---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspe3210.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Initial Measurement" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Debt Issuance Costs, Discounts, and Premiums" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Subsequent Measurement — the Effective Interest Method" },
        { id: "s6", label: "THE DISTINCTIVE CHOICE — Convertible Debt Bifurcation" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Extinguishment of Debt" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Current/Non-Current Classification — Cross-Referenced to Section 1510" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Amortizing a Debt Discount Under the Effective Interest Method" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Worked Example — Electing Not to Bifurcate Convertible Debt" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Relationship to IFRS (IAS 32/IFRS 9)" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Financing obligations extending beyond the short term</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 3210 governs the RECOGNITION, MEASUREMENT, and PRESENTATION of LONG-term debt — BORROWINGS due TO be settled BEYOND one YEAR (or the NORMAL operating CYCLE, per Section 1510). GENUINELY distinctively, THIS Section OFFERS an EXPLICIT accounting POLICY choice FOR convertible debt, RATHER than the MANDATORY component-SPLIT approach IFRS requires (Section 6).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Borrowings maturing beyond the short term</div><div class="principle">This Section applies TO long-TERM notes PAYABLE, BONDS, debentures, MORTGAGES, and SIMILAR borrowings — THE current PORTION of long-TERM debt is CLASSIFIED per SECTION 1510'S own CURRENT/non-current RULES (see the COMPANION poster).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Initial Measurement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Fair value at issuance, net of transaction costs</div><div class="text-supporting">LONG-term debt IS initially MEASURED at ITS fair VALUE (GENERALLY the PROCEEDS received), NET of DIRECTLY attributable TRANSACTION costs — CONSISTENT with the GENERAL initial MEASUREMENT approach ALSO used INTERNATIONALLY.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Debt Issuance Costs, Discounts, and Premiums</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Netted against the debt, amortized over its term</div><div class="text-supporting">DEBT issuance COSTS, discounts, AND premiums are NETTED against the CARRYING amount OF the debt (RATHER than presented SEPARATELY as an ASSET or DEFERRED item), AMORTIZED over the TERM of the DEBT using the EFFECTIVE interest METHOD.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Subsequent Measurement — the Effective Interest Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Amortized cost, using a constant effective rate</div><div class="text-supporting">LONG-term debt is SUBSEQUENTLY measured AT amortized COST using the EFFECTIVE interest METHOD — RECOGNIZING interest EXPENSE at a CONSTANT rate ON the DEBT'S outstanding CARRYING amount, GRADUALLY amortizing ANY discount, PREMIUM, or ISSUANCE cost OVER the DEBT'S remaining TERM.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>THE DISTINCTIVE CHOICE — Convertible Debt Bifurcation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Split accounting is elective, not mandatory</div><div class="text-supporting">FOR a CONVERTIBLE debt INSTRUMENT (a COMPOUND financial INSTRUMENT WITH both LIABILITY and EQUITY components), ASPE PERMITS an ENTERPRISE to ELECT EITHER (a) BIFURCATE the INSTRUMENT into ITS separate LIABILITY and EQUITY components (USING a RESIDUAL-value approach, SIMILAR to the SPLIT accounting IFRS requires), OR (b) ACCOUNT for the ENTIRE instrument AS a single LIABILITY, WITH NO separate EQUITY component RECOGNIZED at ALL. THIS is a GENUINELY distinctive ACCOUNTING policy CHOICE — INTERNATIONALLY, IAS 32 MANDATES the SPLIT-accounting approach FOR compound INSTRUMENTS with NO single-liability ALTERNATIVE permitted.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Extinguishment of Debt</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A gain or loss recognized immediately</div><div class="text-supporting">UPON extinguishing DEBT (e.g. EARLY repayment OR a SUBSTANTIAL modification OF terms), the ENTERPRISE recognizes a GAIN or LOSS FOR the DIFFERENCE between the DEBT'S carrying AMOUNT and the CONSIDERATION paid TO extinguish IT, INCLUDING any UNAMORTIZED issuance COSTS, discounts, OR premiums.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Current/Non-Current Classification — Cross-Referenced to Section 1510</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Including the callable debt rule for covenant violations</div><div class="text-supporting">THE portion OF long-TERM debt DUE within ONE year (or the OPERATING cycle) is CLASSIFIED as CURRENT — INCLUDING debt SUBJECT to the DISTINCTIVE callable-DEBT rule DISCUSSED in SECTION 1510 (see the COMPANION poster), WHERE a COVENANT violation CAN push an ENTIRE long-TERM balance INTO current LIABILITIES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Amortizing a Debt Discount Under the Effective Interest Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Interest expense exceeding the stated coupon rate</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A bond issued at a discount</div><div class="wk-body">A company issues a $1,000,000 face-value bond for $950,000 net proceeds (after issuance costs), carrying a 6% stated coupon rate. The effective interest rate, given the discount, is 6.8%.</div><div class="wk-answer">FIRST-year INTEREST expense = $950,000 × 6.8% = <strong>$64,600</strong> — EXCEEDING the $1,000,000 × 6% = $60,000 CASH interest PAID, WITH the $4,600 DIFFERENCE amortizing THE discount, GRADUALLY increasing the BOND'S carrying AMOUNT toward ITS $1,000,000 face VALUE by MATURITY.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — Electing Not to Bifurcate Convertible Debt</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A simpler, single-liability presentation</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Convertible notes issued to private investors</div><div class="wk-body">A private company issues $2,000,000 of convertible notes to investors, carrying both a liability component (the debt) and an embedded equity component (the conversion feature). The company elects the single-liability alternative.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY recognizes the FULL $2,000,000 as a <strong>SINGLE liability</strong>, WITH NO separate EQUITY component RECOGNIZED — a GENUINELY simpler PRESENTATION than the BIFURCATED, split-ACCOUNTING approach IFRS WOULD require FOR the SAME instrument.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 3210 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Terms and conditions of significant long-term debt, including interest rates and maturity dates</span><span>Aggregate maturities of long-term debt for each of the next several years</span><span>Accounting policy elected for convertible debt (bifurcated or single-liability)</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether to bifurcate convertible debt or account for it as a single liability</span><span>Whether a debt modification is substantial enough to constitute an extinguishment</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Effective interest rate underlying the amortized cost calculation</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS (IAS 32/IFRS 9)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 3210 vs IAS 32/IFRS 9</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 3210</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 32/IFRS 9</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Amortized cost / effective interest method</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Convertible debt bifurcation</span><span>Genuine policy choice</span><span>MANDATORY split accounting</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">THE convertible-DEBT bifurcation CHOICE is the SINGLE most SIGNIFICANT divergence — the CORE amortized-COST mechanics are OTHERWISE thoroughly CONVERGED.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every long-term debt event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Interest expense (effective interest method)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Constant rate on outstanding carrying amount</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Gain/loss on extinguishment</span><span><span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Recognized immediately</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1510</span><span>Current Assets and Current Liabilities — supplies the current/non-current classification and callable debt rule applied to this Section's borrowings</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3251</span><span>Equity — governs the equity component of a convertible instrument, where bifurcation is elected</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Effective interest method</div><div class="glossary-def">A method allocating interest expense at a constant rate on a debt's outstanding carrying amount, gradually amortizing any discount, premium, or issuance cost.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Compound financial instrument</div><div class="glossary-def">An instrument containing both a liability and an equity component, such as convertible debt.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe3210 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
